\pard\ql\par
\pard\ql{\fs16 Time is measured in years and centered within benchmark, so the intercept is the frontier at each benchmark's own reference date. cost drop, %/yr is 100*(1 - exp(-b_time / b_ln cost)): the percentage fall in the cost of a fixed accuracy level per year, positive when cost is falling. Linear specification only -- with the quadratic's ln cost x time term the cost slope moves with date, so no single rate describes the column.  No standard errors: the response is the empirical Pareto frontier P_t(c) sampled at the nodes of the envelope's fixed cost-date grid, and grid nodes are not observations. N is the nodes at which the frontier is defined; they resample a few dozen staircase corners, so N measures resolution, not information. No quadratic-versus-linear test: there is no likelihood to test and no sampling distribution to appeal to.}\par
